---
title: "Night market chase"
note: "Three fast cuts in eight seconds: timestamps, cut verbs, a shaking camera and a fast pan. Tests whether H3 keeps the same thief across cuts. One shouted line in Cantonese."
tags: [h3, action, cuts]
---
@h3 t2va 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic
$thief = __creature[mammal]__

SHOT 3s | tracking, fast
A crowded night market on a bridge in monsoon rain, paper lanterns swinging. A $thief sprints between the stalls with a glowing paper lantern in its mouth, knocking over a crate of oranges.
SFX: rain hammers on tarpaulins; oranges bounce across wet planks

SHOT 2s | cut, shake strongly
A stall owner in a yellow raincoat vaulting over his counter to give chase.
OWNER (hoarse middle-aged male voice): [Cantonese] 站住!
SFX: a metal gong clatters to the ground

SHOT 3s | cut, pan right, large, fast
The $thief leaping off the bridge railing onto a passing boat and vanishing under its canopy, the lantern still glowing.

MUSIC: fast taiko drums and a driving upright bass at a quick tempo, building in volume
